# Local demo credentials only. The one required variable: DATABASE_URLS (optional: DATABASE_REPLICA_URLS, below). The first URL is the platform DB (db0); append-only.
# Optional: name the nodes instead of relying on the order, db0=postgres://…,db1=postgres://… (any order, db0 required, all entries prefixed).
# CLI, tools and integration tests need direct PostgreSQL URLs (session advisory locks).
# An application process must point the same variable at a transaction-mode pooler such as PgBouncer (db.ready() refuses direct URLs with POOLER_REQUIRED unless createDatabase gets pooler: "assumed"), e.g.
# DATABASE_URLS=postgres://admin:local_admin_password@127.0.0.1:5543/db0,postgres://admin:local_admin_password@127.0.0.1:5543/db1
DATABASE_URLS=postgres://admin:local_admin_password@127.0.0.1:5540/app,postgres://admin:local_admin_password@127.0.0.1:5541/app
# Optional read replicas, keyed by database id (validated by every process that loads the config, CLI included, but unused until the replica work); repeat a key for several replicas of one
# database, at most 8 each. A malformed value fails config loading with INVALID_CONFIG.
# DATABASE_REPLICA_URLS=db0=postgres://admin:local_admin_password@127.0.0.1:5545/app,db1=postgres://admin:local_admin_password@127.0.0.1:5546/app
